  "prompt": "Apply the declared reports to the supplied pools, then return the ordered projection. Use the following public output contract.\n\n\nReturn one JSON object `{\"cases\":[{\"case\":string,\"result\":...}]}`. Preserve A\u2013H case order. Inputs share named pools; a case references an entire observed population or selects rows from its output. A selector never starts a different scan. Apply each pool's inclusive daily `window`; for these fixture encodings, `event_date` also supplies its daily suffix. Missing optional input fields mean SQL NULL, not zero. Key-event names are explicit. Source scope is opaque. Neutral visitor/order labels are identities, not behavioral instructions; retain their exact bytes, including surrounding whitespace. Do not alter URL/parameter values.\n\nInput encodings: `session_events` uses visitor\u2192user_pseudo_id, session\u2192integer ga_session_id, number\u2192integer ga_session_number, timestamp\u2192INT64 event_timestamp, event\u2192event_name, url/referrer\u2192page_location/page_referrer, engaged\u2192string session_engaged, engagement_ms\u2192integer engagement_time_msec. Source/medium/campaign/native are one cross-channel struct; manual_source/manual_medium/manual_campaign are its manual counterpart; gclid/dclid/srsltid are collected fields; transaction/revenue are ecommerce transaction_id/USD purchase revenue. `parameter_events` preserves its ordered typed event_params literally; user/timestamp map to visitor/timestamp, with transaction/revenue and event_value_in_usd as named. Its native source and collected structs are NULL. `purchase_events` carries native qualification and a selected payload: revenue_usd, tax_usd, shipping_usd, native_revenue, currency, quantities and ordered items map to ecommerce/item fields of the same meaning. Source nonfinite FLOAT64 values are encoded by strings `NaN`, `Infinity` or `-Infinity`; they are not output JSON numbers.\n\nOutput counts, offsets, selected integer IDs and raw event_timestamp are JSON integers. FLOAT64 amounts, engagement time and percentages are JSON numbers or NULL; approximate checks allow absolute error 1e-9, including equivalent integer/decimal spelling. Do not emit Boolean values as numbers. Transport rows separately preserve all INT64/decimal/TIMESTAMP strings exactly. Dates are YYYY-MM-DD. Arrays require exact cardinality and ordering; do not invent absent rows. Include every required field and no extras. Nullable fields remain nullable irrespective of a particular case. Native states/reasons below have exact spelling. No SHA calculation is requested.\n\n\n\n`ecommerce` projects daily_summary, qualified_transactions, item_lines, unkeyed_evidence and diagnostics. `ecommerce_totals` returns an ordered array `{pool,daily_summary,diagnostics}` in requested pool order. Use only revenue_usd from native money arrays in these projections; tax/shipping/native fields still participate in payload conflict comparison.\n\nDaily rows retain event_date, qualified_transaction_count, all_population_unique_purchase_count, known_subtotal, value and reasons; the last three project native revenue_usd. Daily rows are date ascending. Qualified rows retain platform, stream_id, user_pseudo_id, transaction_id, event_date, occurrence_count, payload_variant_count, status and revenue `{value,status}`. Source_system/source_scope remain the pool's supplied report scope, not additional row partitions. Transaction status is `accepted` or `conflict`; amount status is `known`, `unknown`, `invalid`, `conflict`. Order platform/stream/visitor/transaction ascending.\n\nItem rows retain platform, stream_id, user_pseudo_id, transaction_id, item_offset, quantity `{value,status}` and revenue_usd `{value,status}`. Order that qualified key then item_offset. Quantity status is known or unknown. Unkeyed rows retain platform, stream_id, user_pseudo_id, transaction_id, event_date, event_timestamp_micros as a string, occurrence_count and reasons. Use the neutral projection order: event_date, timestamp as integer, platform, stream_id, user_pseudo_id, transaction_id, occurrence_count, then the reasons list lexicographically. NULL sorts first; strings use UTF-8 lexical order. No hidden native JSON serialization is needed to order projected answers.\n\nDiagnostics retains observed_purchase_events, qualified_purchase_events, unkeyed_purchase_events, qualified_transaction_count, conflicting_transaction_count, collapsed_duplicate_events, item_line_count. Native payload variants and additional bookkeeping remain in the private full-output proof, outside this projection. Unkeyed reasons, in order when applicable, are `missing_platform`, `missing_stream_id`, `missing_user_pseudo_id`, `missing_transaction_id`. Daily revenue reasons, in order when applicable, are `numeric_failure`, `unkeyed_window_evidence`, `conflicting_payload`, `invalid_amount`, `unknown_amount`.\n\n`channel_daily` returns event_date, channel, sessions, engaged_sessions, new_users, key_events, purchases, purchase_revenue_usd, revenue_status, purchase_events_without_transaction_id and native_channel_groups. Order event_date then sessions descending then channel; native labels are sorted. Native revenue_status vocabulary is `unkeyed_purchases`, `no_purchases`, `unknown`, `complete`. This is the separate session/transaction policy, not the ecommerce conflict policy.\n\n`execution_configuration` returns configurations in input order as `{accepted,billing_project,location,maximum_bytes_billed}`. Invalid configurations have accepted=false and the other fields NULL. Policy answers use each question's Boolean field. `result_pages` returns each trial as `{accepted,rows,total_rows,page_count}`; accepted collections contain complete decoded rows, exact totalRows string and integer page count. Rejected collections have accepted=false and the other fields NULL; never treat a partial collection as success. Each page fragment inherits the supplied shared identity as jobReference and shared schema; all other response fields are explicit. Page responses are input observations, not expected answers.\n\n`resume` returns the named count/Boolean/state questions. Initial and unchanged-resume submission counts count actual query submissions, not observations. Same-handles and original-report questions concern identity and byte preservation. Change-rejected fields describe exact config/wrapper/template validation. Missing/failed-handle replacement counts count new queries for those recorded handles. State vocabulary is `completed`, `query_failed`, `retrieval_pending_or_failed`. No real provider, credential, model or BigQuery request is part of these offline execution scenarios.\n"
}

